WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.930
Week 17: Preterite: Completed Events. report what happened sequence completed actions ask follow-up questions

2
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:14.132
Mission brief. Deliver a concise incident report with who, what, when, where, and outcome.

3
00:00:14.132 --> 00:00:23.537
Preparation. Select ten useful words, three linking expressions, and two repair phrases. Plan points rather than a memorized paragraph.

4
00:00:23.537 --> 00:00:31.317
Performance. Complete the task once for fluency, review the evidence, then repeat it for greater clarity and accuracy.

5
00:00:31.317 --> 00:00:39.845
After-action review. Record what succeeded, what blocked communication, and the single change that will matter most on the next attempt.

6
00:00:39.845 --> 00:01:07.596
Model language. Voy a presentar un informe conciso. — I am going to present a concise report. Explico quién, qué, cuándo y dónde. — I explain who, what, when, and where. También incluyo el resultado final. — I also include the final outcome. El informe no debe ser demasiado largo. — The report shouldn't be too long. Termino con una conclusión clara. — I finish with a clear conclusion.

7
00:01:07.596 --> 00:01:17.494
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
